1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You'll blame winter for this.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
But summer already did the damage.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,200
Heat speeds up the chemical
reaction inside a battery.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,200
It corrodes the plates
and evaporates the fluid —

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,000
quietly, all summer,
under a hot engine hood.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,500
The first sign shows up
on a cold morning —

7
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,200
a slow crank,
dim headlights at idle.

8
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:24,000
But by then the battery had been
weakening since July.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Batteries usually last
three to five years.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,300
Cleveland heat shortens that.

11
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:30,000
Free check before the first
cold morning strands you.
